<title>LEBANON: Lebanese 12-, 24-mo treasury bill yields dip.</title>
<headline>Lebanese 12-, 24-mo treasury bill yields dip.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Longer-term yields fell slightly on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its October 10 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		    Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  14.10 (14.10)	     14.61  (14.61)</p>
<p>    Six months	    15.60 (15.60)	     16.92  (16.92)</p>
<p>    12 months	     15.11 (15.12)	     17.79  (17.80)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 21.64  (21.66)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
</text>
